Changelog: 30-10-2026 16:11:24

Release 2.0.0.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 14:53:00

Breaking. A game's Steam shortcut starts the app's play mode (owner, 30-10-2026: "Hold View + Menu, everywhere"):
PPSSPP-Manager.exe --play --fullscreen --pause-menu-exit "<game>", which starts PPSSPP in its folder and ends with it,
so its Steam number and artwork names change. A shortcut made before, which starts PPSSPPWindows64.exe itself, is
still the game's: it shows (Update Steam), and Y Update Steam writes it again (shortcuts.outdated()).

Changelog: 30-10-2026 14:53:00

Added. Hold View and Menu together for two seconds to quit a game (core's play mode): PPSSPP closes as its window
would, from Steam's library, X Play or without Steam. The line at the bottom says so when a game starts ("In the game,
hold View and Menu together to quit."), and Your games' information and the wiki chapter. LT (or the guide button)
still opens PPSSPP's pause menu, whose Exit ends the game too.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 13:35:58

Breaking. The Open Steam row above the games in Your games is gone (owner, 30-10-2026): Steam's library opens
from the portal, RT Steam.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 13:35:58

Added. On a device without Steam (not installed, or never started), X Play starts the game in PPSSPP itself, full
screen, with the command its Steam shortcut has (shortcuts.command(), core's platform.start_program() outside the
app's bundle; owner, 30-10-2026: a fallback, as a game cannot be played without Steam otherwise). Without PPSSPP
installed it says to install it first. With Steam installed X plays through Steam as before.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 12:54:34

Fixed. Steam started by the app signs in (core, owner, 30-10-2026): X Play and the restart after Steam's shortcuts
changed started steam.exe by the lower-case name in Steam's registry key, and a Steam started so never signed in, its
login window off the screen; it is started by its name as on the disk now, outside the app's bundle. The information
popup's text box is as high as its text, up to 0.7 of the window: a text with "[PSP] <title>" in it was measured as
HTML and kept four lines high.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 01:30:27

Release 1.0.1.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 23:14:12

Fixed. Update Steam starts Steam again signed in (core's with_steam_closed(): a plain steam.exe on Windows; owner,
29-10-2026): the steam.exe -silent it started never signed in, so a game's Play and Open Steam did nothing until
Steam was started by hand. The status line says Steam was started again, signed in.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 21:56:04

Release 1.0.0.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 21:43:25

Added. X Play on Your games starts the game the focus is on through Steam, by its shortcut's appid
(steam://rungameid/), Steam first when it is not open (owner, 29-10-2026: a game started from the manager); a game
not in Steam yet says how to put it there. An Open Steam row above the games opens Steam's library in Big Picture
mode. The folder browser opens in the game folder added last, while it is there (owner, 29-10-2026: the folder
remembered after it was chosen).

Fixed. The Log pane's newest lines ran off the pane's top (owner, 29-10-2026): they are a view of their own now, the
newest line in sight. A long information text scrolls (core's popup), and the popup closes with B Close in its legend
instead of a big button.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 17:05:12

Release 0.1.1.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 16:36:08

Fixed. A removable drive without a card (an empty SD or card-reader slot keeps its drive letter, and Windows raises
when asked about it: WinError 1005, no recognized file system) is left out of the folders offered as + Add, instead of
ending the app while it lists them (found on the development PC's card reader, 29-10-2026); core's folder browser
leaves it out of the places the same way.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 14:35:18

Release 0.1.0.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 10:26:43

Added. The BC250 suite's PPSSPP Manager on the portable window (owner, 29-10-2026: "I want to start with PPSSPP
Manager"), laid out as PCSX2 Manager: four cards, PPSSPP, Your games, Settings and Log, the actions with a controller
button in the row at the bottom. A Install downloads PPSSPP 1.20.4 for Windows (PPSSPP-v1.20.4-Windows-x64.zip, 20
MB) from PPSSPP's release on GitHub, checks it against the pinned SHA-256 and unpacks it into
%LOCALAPPDATA%\windows-portable-suite\windows-portable-ppsspp\emulator\, in PPSSPP's portable mode (no installed.txt:
its memory stick, with the settings, saves and save states, in memstick\ beside it); X Remove PPSSPP, with a second
press, deletes only the files the release brought; Y Update when an older PPSSPP is there. Your games: the PSP disc
images (ISO, CSO, CHD) and memory stick games (EBOOT.PBP) in the chosen folders and on PPSSPP's memory stick, read as
the BC250 app reads them; played from Steam, never from the app (owner, 29-10-2026), alone and full screen
(--fullscreen --pause-menu-exit: PPSSPP's own window never shows, LT opens its pause menu and Exit ends PPSSPP); A
Steam mark and Y Update Steam put them in Steam as "[PSP] <title>", with the game's own pictures and a cover from
SteamGridDB with the suite's key (RB Steam artwork); LB Folders, with the app's own folder browser for the controller
(core's browse), where Windows' folder window cannot be used. Settings in four tabs (Picture, Game, Controller, On
screen: 15 settings of ppsspp.ini, PPSSPP's own keys and defaults), never written while PPSSPP runs; PPSSPP's notice
of a newer release turned off. The Log: the memory stick's saves and save states, and the app's log; A View log (or a
tap) shows the whole log in the app. Every action is in the row at the bottom, A too, and no pane holds a pill
(owner, 29-10-2026). The buttons are the suite's (owner, 29-10-2026): B goes back (from a pane to its card, from a
page to where it came from; on a card it does nothing), View (⧉) exits the app and Menu (☰) opens the information of
the pane that shows; B on the folders goes back to the games, on Steam artwork to Your games. In a pane the d-pad
stays in it, and only B goes back to the cards (core's rule). No path on the screen or in the log shows the user's
name: the user's folders as %LOCALAPPDATA% and %USERPROFILE% (owner, 29-10-2026). Not carried over yet: the BC250
app's Rename files.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 10:11:34

